u\mu}\circ r_{\mu\lambda}=r_{
u\lambda}$ for $\lambda\le\mu\le
u$, and for every $\lambda$ a local homomorphism $\pi_\lambda:R_\lambda	o R$ with $\pi_\mu\circ r_{\mu\lambda}=\pi_\lambda$, such that (1) $(R,(\pi_\lambda)_{\lambda\in\Lambda})$ is a colimit [def-weil-pbc-category-colimit] of the system $(R_\lambda,r_{\mu\lambda})$ in the category of commutative rings, and (2) every $R_\lambda$ is essentially of finite type over $\mathbf Z$ [def-weil-pbc-essentially-finite-type-algebra].
